prompt:
Use Three.js to implement an advanced chair configurator. Load SheenChair.glb and support material switching, color selection, and saving/loading configurations.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/SheenChair.glb;
(2) Display the model centered;

[Material Selection]
(3) Three material buttons (with ids "matLeather"/"matFabric"/"matVelvet", respectively);
(4) Leather: roughness=0.3, metalness=0.1;
(5) Fabric: roughness=0.9, metalness=0;
(6) Velvet: roughness=0.7, metalness=0.05, with a sheen effect;

[Color Selection]
(7) A color picker (id="cushionColor", type="color") changes the cushion color;
(8) Locate the mesh representing the cushion in the model (determine it by name or position);

[Leg Style]
(9) Toggle button (id="legStyle"): wood (brown, roughness=0.8) / metal (silver, metalness=0.9);
(10) Modify the material of the chair-leg mesh;

[Save/Load]
(11) The "Save" button (id="saveBtn") stores the current configuration as JSON in localStorage;
(12) The "Load" button (id="loadBtn") reads the configuration from localStorage and applies it;
(13) Configuration contents: {material, color, legStyle};

[OrbitControls]
(14) Support rotating the view;

[HUD Display]
(15) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Material type (id="materialType")
  - Color hex value (id="colorValue")
  - Number of saved configurations (id="savedCount")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - materialType: string
  - colorHex: string
  - legStyle: string ("wood"/"metal")
  - savedConfigs: number

Output a standalone HTML file.
